  "description": "KASKAT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H103 Co3 Dy3 N3 O28 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.271-3.923 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.86-111.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co3Dy3(OH)4(O2CCMe3)6(teaH)3(H2O)3](NO3)2·H2O (C48H105Co3Dy3N5O35). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(II).",
